<title>SWEDEN: Scania says French strike halts output.</title>
<headline>Scania says French strike halts output.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish truck producer Scania said it had been forced to halt production at its truck production plant in Angers, France, because of a strike by French transport workers.</p>
<p>&quot;As a consequence of the conflict we have been forced to stop production at the Angers assembly plant today,&quot; said Scania spokesman Hans Rubenstein.  </p>
<p>Scania said it had been unable to obtain components. The Angers plant produces 35 to 40 trucks a day.</p>
<p>He said the plant would remain closed until the strike was over.</p>
<p>Other Scania plants in the Netherlands and in Sweden were experiencing some disruption because of the French dispute and truck drivers' industrial action in Denmark, he added.</p>
<p>-- Simon Haydon, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
